(SUPERVISED AND UNSUPERVISED LEARNING) '
T*
(Supervised learning algorithms are trained using labeled datasets, where the desired output is known.) '
(Common algorithms include Linear Regression, Support Vector Machines, and Decision Trees.) '
(Supervised learning is widely used for classification and regression tasks like spam detection and price prediction.) '
T*
(Unsupervised learning uses unlabeled data to discover hidden patterns and clusters without human guidance.) '
(Examples include K-Means Clustering and Principal Component Analysis \(PCA\).) '
ET
endstream
endobj
