(RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION \(RAG\)) '
T*
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is an architectural framework that improves the accuracy of Large Language Models \(LLMs\).) '
(Instead of relying solely on training weights, RAG retrieves relevant facts from an external knowledge base) '
(or private document collection before generating a response.) '
T*
(Key advantages of RAG include:) '
(1. Reduction in hallucination by grounding responses in verified source texts.) '
(2. Access to domain-specific and up-to-date data without expensive fine-tuning.) '
(3. Verifiable source citations and page transparency for users.) '
ET
endstream
